From 1f2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armbian Build <build@armbian.local>
Date: Tue, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] u-boot: allow rockusb entry on empty eMMC (no GPT)

When the recovery key is pressed, vendor U-Boot runs
`rockusb 0 $devtype $devnum`. do_rkusb() in cmd/rockusb.c already
appends ":0" for nvme/scsi devnum 0 so rkusb_init() tolerates a
missing partition table via allow_whole_dev -- mmc was left out.

On an empty eMMC (no GPT), part_get_info_efi fails, rkusb_init
returns -1, do_rkusb fails, and cmd/download.c falls back to
`rbrom`, soft-rebooting the SoC. SPI NOR still has a valid IDB,
so the BootROM reloads U-Boot, the recovery key is still held,
and the cycle repeats forever -- RKDevTool never sees a Loader.

Extend the existing ":0" fallback to mmc 0.

---
 patch/u-boot/legacy/u-boot-radxa-rk35xx/board_recomputer-rk3576-devkit/0008-rk3576-rockusb-allow-empty-emmc.patch | 32 ++++++++++
 patch/u-boot/legacy/u-boot-radxa-rk35xx/board_recomputer-rk3588-devkit/0008-rk3588-rockusb-allow-empty-emmc.patch | 32 ++++++++++
